Error: Package: MariaDB-server-10.11.19-1.el7_9.x86_64 (mariadb) Requires: pv` — pv was not resolvable from the repos enabled at that point.\"},{\"source\":\"yum_install4.log, all 3 nodes, ~21:38-21:41\",\"finding\":\"After pv became resolvable, the install failed later at GPG key import: `Retrieving key from https://archive.mariadb.org/mariadb-10.11/yum/RPM-GPG-KEY-MariaDB` then `GPG key retrieval failed: [Errno 14] HTTPS Error 404 - Not Found`.\"},{\"source\":\"yum_install5.log, node1 only, 21:42:31\",\"finding\":\"A third attempt shows `Complete!` on node1 (install succeeded, including pv, rsync, socat, stunnel, replacement of mariadb-libs). No node2/node3 result for this final attempt appears in the redacted record selection.\"},{\"source\":\"Attempt termination metadata\",\"finding\":\"Lease expired at 2026-09-04T21:42:57Z, ~26 seconds after the node1 install completion timestamp (21:42:31). No later records (Galera config, cluster bootstrap, mysql actions, service stop/start) appear anywhere in the selected records.\"},{\"source\":\"Audit summary counts\",\"finding\":\"113 total command records, 56 completed, 57 requested (many still in-flight/unresolved), consistent with the run being cut off mid-install rather than completing normally.\"}],\"likely_causes\":[{\"cause\":\"The RHEL7 image's default enabled repos did not include EPEL (source of pv) until the executor fixed repo config between install attempt 3 and 4 — the first failure is a missing-dependency issue from incomplete repo setup, not real package unavailability.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"cause\":\"The MariaDB 10.11 official YUM repo's GPG key URL (archive.mariadb.org/mariadb-10.11/yum/RPM-GPG-KEY-MariaDB) returned HTTP 404 at run time — either a transient MariaDB CDN/mirror issue or a stale/incorrect key path for this 10.11.19 build.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"},{\"cause\":\"The executor used a serial, poll-with-sleep pattern (60-90s sleeps, repeated per node, repeated across 3 failed attempts) for package installation, burning nearly the whole lease on OS-level setup before any Galera-specific work could begin, leaving no time margin for the actual task.\",\"confidence\":\"high\"}],\"next_attempt_guidance\":[\"Before running the real yum install, pre-validate repo setup on one node only: confirm EPEL is enabled (yum repolist shows epel) and pv resolves (yum list pv), and confirm the MariaDB repo GPG key URL is reachable (curl -I) before fanning the install out to all 3 nodes.\",\"If the MariaDB.org GPG key URL 404s again, don't retry blindly — verify the current documented key URL/path for the 10.11 series, import from a locally cached copy, or use gpgcheck=0 only as a last-resort with awareness of the tradeoff.\",\"Run OS package installation on all 3 nodes in parallel/background (launch then poll with short tail checks) rather than sequential 60-90s blocking sleeps repeated per node per attempt.\",\"Budget time explicitly: if yum/repo issues aren't resolved within roughly the first 10% of the available lease window, stop repeating near-identical install attempts and switch strategy (different mirror, offline RPMs, different base image).\",\"The actual task — Galera cluster bootstrap, safe full-cluster shutdown, wsrep-new-cluster recovery bootstrap from the node with highest seqno in grastate.dat, rejoin of the other two nodes, and write-durability verification — was never attempted in this run; treat this postmortem as covering only the environment-setup phase.\"],\"summary\":\"Attempt 1 never reached Galera cluster configuration, data seeding, or the actual cold-restart maintenance procedure. The entire observed command window (21:34–21:42 UTC) was consumed retrying `yum install` for MariaDB-server on RHEL7 across node1–node3, and the cluster lease expired (21:42:57) roughly 26 seconds after the first node finally reported a successful install. No evidence exists that MariaDB/Galera was ever started, joined, had data written, or was shut down/restarted.\"}","structured_output":{"evidence":[{"source":"yum_install3.log, all 3 nodes, ~21:34-21:36","finding":"`yum install` failed with `Error: Package: MariaDB-server-10.11.19-1.el7_9.x86_64 (mariadb) Requires: pv` — pv was not resolvable from the repos enabled at that point."},{"source":"yum_install4.log, all 3 nodes, ~21:38-21:41","finding":"After pv became resolvable, the install failed later at GPG key import: `Retrieving key from https://archive.mariadb.org/mariadb-10.11/yum/RPM-GPG-KEY-MariaDB` then `GPG key retrieval failed: [Errno 14] HTTPS Error 404 - Not Found`."},{"source":"yum_install5.log, node1 only, 21:42:31","finding":"A third attempt shows `Complete!` on node1 (install succeeded, including pv, rsync, socat, stunnel, replacement of mariadb-libs). No node2/node3 result for this final attempt appears in the redacted record selection."},{"source":"Attempt termination metadata","finding":"Lease expired at 2026-09-04T21:42:57Z, ~26 seconds after the node1 install completion timestamp (21:42:31). No later records (Galera config, cluster bootstrap, mysql actions, service stop/start) appear anywhere in the selected records."},{"source":"Audit summary counts","finding":"113 total command records, 56 completed, 57 requested (many still in-flight/unresolved), consistent with the run being cut off mid-install rather than completing normally."}],"likely_causes":[{"cause":"The RHEL7 image's default enabled repos did not include EPEL (source of pv) until the executor fixed repo config between install attempt 3 and 4 — the first failure is a missing-dependency issue from incomplete repo setup, not real package unavailability.","confidence":"high"},{"cause":"The MariaDB 10.11 official YUM repo's GPG key URL (archive.mariadb.org/mariadb-10.11/yum/RPM-GPG-KEY-MariaDB) returned HTTP 404 at run time — either a transient MariaDB CDN/mirror issue or a stale/incorrect key path for this 10.11.19 build.","confidence":"medium"},{"cause":"The executor used a serial, poll-with-sleep pattern (60-90s sleeps, repeated per node, repeated across 3 failed attempts) for package installation, burning nearly the whole lease on OS-level setup before any Galera-specific work could begin, leaving no time margin for the actual task.","confidence":"high"}],"next_attempt_guidance":["Before running the real yum install, pre-validate repo setup on one node only: confirm EPEL is enabled (yum repolist shows epel) and pv resolves (yum list pv), and confirm the MariaDB repo GPG key URL is reachable (curl -I) before fanning the install out to all 3 nodes.","If the MariaDB.org GPG key URL 404s again, don't retry blindly — verify the current documented key URL/path for the 10.11 series, import from a locally cached copy, or use gpgcheck=0 only as a last-resort with awareness of the tradeoff.","Run OS package installation on all 3 nodes in parallel/background (launch then poll with short tail checks) rather than sequential 60-90s blocking sleeps repeated per node per attempt.","Budget time explicitly: if yum/repo issues aren't resolved within roughly the first 10% of the available lease window, stop repeating near-identical install attempts and switch strategy (different mirror, offline RPMs, different base image).","The actual task — Galera cluster bootstrap, safe full-cluster shutdown, wsrep-new-cluster recovery bootstrap from the node with highest seqno in grastate.dat, rejoin of the other two nodes, and write-durability verification — was never attempted in this run; treat this postmortem as covering only the environment-setup phase."],"summary":"Attempt 1 never reached Galera cluster configuration, data seeding, or the actual cold-restart maintenance procedure. The entire observed command window (21:34–21:42 UTC) was consumed retrying `yum install` for MariaDB-server on RHEL7 across node1–node3, and the cluster lease expired (21:42:57) roughly 26 seconds after the first node finally reported a successful install. No evidence exists that MariaDB/Galera was ever 